  "visual_findings": [
    "The fixed fold diagnostic revisited the smaller hand-B inward yaw offset -40 with support offset -40, then changed only servo 6 from 1740 to 1680 us and back. Servo 5 returned next, followed by the support. All six transitions had paired front and top reviews before progression.",
    "The support-only entry and return visibly raised and lowered the puppet body. The isolated servo-5 and servo-6 edges did not produce a clearly distinguishable change in the visible elbow/hand articulation at this view and amplitude. This does not prove a failed motor, nor a measured deadband.",
    "Hand B continued to overlap or be obscured by the body. No wrist coordinates were guessed for the hidden hand; neither independent hand-side change nor elbow folding was verified.",
    "The prior -80 yaw trial had already caused visible torso foreshortening. This trial did not expand beyond the smaller -40 yaw offset or attempt head-top crossing, head yaw compensation or a combined freeform performance.",
    "No obvious detached rod, curtain exit or rod interference was visible in the paired images, but force and full 3D clearance were not measured. Tiger outputs stayed disabled.",
    "The compiled closed command route ended normally at the reference pulses with all ten outputs off. Actual shaft angles and exact puppet-joint repeatability remain unknown; the original incident locks were retained."
  ],
